WEBVTT

00:00:15.463 --> 00:00:16.642
It's not a dream.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.739
You ever heard of an
out-Of-Body experience?

00:00:18.774 --> 00:00:20.235
We're spirits...

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:22.645
Of people close to death.

00:00:24.679 --> 00:00:27.620
Your son is dying, and
you're worried about the colt?

00:00:29.008 --> 00:00:31.106
You shoot me in the heart, son!

00:00:33.125 --> 00:00:34.486
You're bringing the
demon here, aren't you?

00:00:34.487 --> 00:00:36.945
Having some stupid, macho showdown!

00:00:37.556 --> 00:00:39.760
If you killed that damn
thing when you had the chance,

00:00:39.771 --> 00:00:41.894
None of this would have happened.

00:00:48.728 --> 00:00:50.282
I want to make a deal.

00:00:51.887 --> 00:00:54.011
You're much prettier than
the last reaper I met.

00:00:54.017 --> 00:00:57.473
I will give you the colt and the
bullet. But you got to help Dean.

00:00:58.865 --> 00:01:00.542
So, we have a deal?

00:01:01.117 --> 00:01:03.341
You still need to sweeten the pot.

00:01:05.706 --> 00:01:07.661
Today is your lucky day, kid.

00:01:09.925 --> 00:01:12.002
You watch out for Sammy, okay?

00:01:20.396 --> 00:01:21.430
Okay.

00:01:21.817 --> 00:01:22.722
Dad?

00:01:26.616 --> 00:01:28.581
Time of death, 10:41 a.M.

00:01:55.015 --> 00:01:57.652
God, I hate clowns. Always creep me out.

00:01:57.657 --> 00:01:59.212
Shh! She likes them.

00:02:08.736 --> 00:02:10.021
Last ride, Nora.

00:02:23.938 --> 00:02:25.610
Look, mom, another clown.

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:33.221
What are you trying to
do, scare your father?

00:02:33.227 --> 00:02:34.222
Honey.

00:02:50.506 --> 00:02:52.262
Look, mom, a clown.

00:02:57.056 --> 00:02:58.621
You missed him.

00:04:52.045 --> 00:04:53.781
Before he...

00:04:54.895 --> 00:04:55.980
Before he...

00:05:00.895 --> 00:05:02.470
Did he say anything to you?

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:06.501
About anything?

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:15.662
No.

00:05:19.646 --> 00:05:20.972
Nothing.

00:06:00.245 --> 00:06:01.681
How's the car coming along?

00:06:01.688 --> 00:06:02.612
Slow.

00:06:03.647 --> 00:06:04.562
Yeah?

00:06:05.867 --> 00:06:07.650
You need any help?

00:06:07.658 --> 00:06:09.203
What? You under a hood?

00:06:09.766 --> 00:06:10.943
I'll pass.

00:06:13.518 --> 00:06:14.713
Need anything else, then?

00:06:17.218 --> 00:06:18.302
Stop it, Sam.

00:06:19.105 --> 00:06:19.951
Stop what?

00:06:19.958 --> 00:06:21.282
Stop asking if I need anything.

00:06:21.297 --> 00:06:23.751
Stop asking if I'm okay. I'm okay.

00:06:24.117 --> 00:06:26.062
Really. I promise.

00:06:29.886 --> 00:06:31.583
All right, Dean, it's just...

00:06:32.886 --> 00:06:36.110
We've been at Bobby's for over a week
now, and you haven't brought up dad once.

00:06:37.776 --> 00:06:39.200
You know what? You're right.

00:06:40.297 --> 00:06:41.232
Come here.

00:06:41.666 --> 00:06:43.540
I'm gonna lay my head
gently on your shoulder.

00:06:43.696 --> 00:06:45.942
Maybe we could cry, hug,

00:06:45.948 --> 00:06:48.451
Maybe even slow dance.
Don't patronize me, Dean.

00:06:48.456 --> 00:06:51.880
Dad is dead, the colt is gone,
and it seems pretty damn likely

00:06:51.886 --> 00:06:54.522
That the demon is behind all of this.
And you're acting like nothing happened.

00:06:54.527 --> 00:06:55.972
What do you want me to say?
Say something, all right?!

00:06:55.976 --> 00:06:59.252
Hell, say anything! Aren't you
angry? Don't you want revenge?

00:06:59.495 --> 00:07:02.860
But all you do is sit out here all day
long buried underneath this damn car.

00:07:02.865 --> 00:07:04.860
Revenge, huh? Sounds good. Yeah!

00:07:05.468 --> 00:07:07.353
Got any leads on where the demon is?

00:07:07.356 --> 00:07:10.130
Making heads or tails of any of
dad's research? 'Cause I sure ain't.

00:07:10.135 --> 00:07:11.792
You know, when we do finally find it...

00:07:11.797 --> 00:07:12.860
Oh,

00:07:12.868 --> 00:07:14.813
No, wait, like you
said, the colt's gone.

00:07:14.816 --> 00:07:16.692
But I'm sure you figured
out another way to kill it.

00:07:16.867 --> 00:07:19.180
We've got nothing, Sam. Nothing, okay?

00:07:19.185 --> 00:07:22.032
The only thing I can do
is I can work on the car.

00:07:24.206 --> 00:07:25.870
Well, we got something, all right?

00:07:26.757 --> 00:07:28.381
It's what I came out here to tell you.

00:07:28.387 --> 00:07:29.851
It's one of dad's old phones.

00:07:29.855 --> 00:07:33.131
It took me a while, but I cracked
his voice mail code. Listen to this.

00:07:37.207 --> 00:07:39.293
<i>John, it's Ellen... Again.</i>

00:07:39.576 --> 00:07:42.360
<i>Look, don't be stubborn. You
know I can help you. Call me.</i>

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:45.440
That message is four months old.

00:07:45.447 --> 00:07:47.231
Dad saved that chick's
message for four months?

00:07:47.235 --> 00:07:48.471
Yeah. Who's Ellen?

00:07:48.478 --> 00:07:50.142
Any mention of her in dad's journal? No,

00:07:50.146 --> 00:07:52.690
But I ran a trace on the
number, and I got an address.

00:07:55.468 --> 00:07:57.262
Ask Bobby if we can use one of his cars.

00:08:08.828 --> 00:08:10.541
This is humiliating.

00:08:14.378 --> 00:08:16.571
I feel like a friggin' soccer mom.

00:08:16.575 --> 00:08:18.860
It's the only car Bobby had running.

00:08:21.838 --> 00:08:23.190
H ello?

00:08:25.206 --> 00:08:26.962
Anybody here? Alright.

00:08:26.967 --> 00:08:29.182
Hey, did you bring the... Of course.

00:08:58.456 --> 00:08:59.782
Hey, buddy?

00:09:03.717 --> 00:09:06.213
I'm guessing that isn't Ellen. Yeah.

00:09:24.208 --> 00:09:26.332
Oh, god, please let that be a rifle.

00:09:27.088 --> 00:09:28.911
No, I'm just real happy to see you.

00:09:29.606 --> 00:09:31.780
Don't move. Not moving. Copy that.

00:09:33.298 --> 00:09:34.771
You should know something, miss.

00:09:34.846 --> 00:09:36.531
When you put a rifle on someone,

00:09:36.535 --> 00:09:38.631
You don't want to put it
right against their back,

00:09:38.835 --> 00:09:41.013
'Cause it makes it real easy to do...

00:09:43.756 --> 00:09:44.782
That!

00:09:45.847 --> 00:09:46.803
Sam!

00:09:47.196 --> 00:09:48.550
I need some help in here.

00:09:48.557 --> 00:09:50.173
I can't see. I can't even see!

00:09:50.328 --> 00:09:51.400
Sorry, Dean.

00:09:52.105 --> 00:09:53.993
I can't right now. I'm a...

00:09:54.517 --> 00:09:55.883
Little  tied up.

00:09:58.595 --> 00:09:59.912
Sam? Dean?

00:10:01.915 --> 00:10:03.003
Winchester?

00:10:04.237 --> 00:10:05.071
Yeah.

00:10:05.978 --> 00:10:07.132
Son of a bitch.

00:10:07.136 --> 00:10:08.422
Mom, you know these guys?

00:10:08.428 --> 00:10:10.750
Yeah,  I think these are
John Winchester's boys.

00:10:14.165 --> 00:10:15.131
Hey, I'm Ellen.

00:10:15.578 --> 00:10:16.833
That's my daughter, Jo.

00:10:18.045 --> 00:10:18.870
Hey.

00:10:19.416 --> 00:10:20.843
You're not gonna hit me again, are you?

00:10:22.018 --> 00:10:23.080
Here you go.

00:10:23.088 --> 00:10:24.032
Thanks.

00:10:27.335 --> 00:10:29.183
You called our dad, said you could help.

00:10:29.816 --> 00:10:30.932
Help with what?

00:10:32.225 --> 00:10:33.740
Well,

00:10:33.898 --> 00:10:35.302
The demon, of course.

00:10:37.137 --> 00:10:38.733
I heard he was closing in on it.

00:10:39.817 --> 00:10:42.353
Was there an article in "the demon
hunter's quarterly" that I missed?

00:10:42.357 --> 00:10:44.011
I mean, who are you? How
do you know about all this?

00:10:44.015 --> 00:10:45.643
Hey, I just run a saloon.

00:10:46.257 --> 00:10:49.752
But hunters have been known
to pass through now and again,

00:10:49.868 --> 00:10:51.893
Including your dad a long time ago.

00:10:51.907 --> 00:10:53.473
John was like family once. Oh yeah?

00:10:53.475 --> 00:10:55.271
I mean he's never mentioned you before.

00:10:56.277 --> 00:10:58.190
You'd have to ask him that.

00:11:01.037 --> 00:11:02.723
So, why exactly do we need your help?

00:11:02.727 --> 00:11:04.550
Hey, don't do me any favors.

00:11:04.866 --> 00:11:06.501
Look, if you don't want my help, fine.

00:11:06.506 --> 00:11:08.533
Don't let the door smack
your ass on the way out.

00:11:08.691 --> 00:11:10.354
But John wouldn't have sent you if...

00:11:16.408 --> 00:11:17.540
He didn't send you.

00:11:24.136 --> 00:11:25.375
He's all right, isn't he?

00:11:27.186 --> 00:11:28.062
No.

00:11:29.545 --> 00:11:30.550
No, he isn't.

00:11:30.937 --> 00:11:33.001
It was the demon, we think.

00:11:34.028 --> 00:11:36.502
It just got him before
he got it, I guess.

00:11:40.338 --> 00:11:42.263
I'm so sorry. It's okay.

00:11:42.488 --> 00:11:43.753
We're all right.

00:11:43.935 --> 00:11:45.883
Really, I know how
close you and your dad...

00:11:45.885 --> 00:11:47.311
Really, lady, I'm fine.

00:11:51.375 --> 00:11:53.532
So, look, if you can help...

00:11:54.806 --> 00:11:56.923
We could use all the help we can get.

00:11:57.297 --> 00:11:58.721
Well, we can't.

00:12:00.027 --> 00:12:01.303
But Ash will.

00:12:01.308 --> 00:12:03.242
Who's Ash? Ash!

00:12:05.025 --> 00:12:06.161
What?

00:12:08.135 --> 00:12:09.752
Closing time?

00:12:11.915 --> 00:12:13.152
That's Ash?

00:12:14.137 --> 00:12:15.153
He's a genius.

00:12:18.005 --> 00:12:20.140
You got to be kidding
me. This guy's no genius.

00:12:20.145 --> 00:12:21.993
He's a Lynyrd Skynyrd roadie.

00:12:22.508 --> 00:12:24.742
I like you. Thanks.

00:12:24.927 --> 00:12:26.211
Just give him a chance.

00:12:31.106 --> 00:12:32.120
All right.

00:12:33.548 --> 00:12:36.840
Well, this stuff's about a
year's worth of our dad's work. So

00:12:37.706 --> 00:12:39.102
Let's see what you make of it.

00:12:49.978 --> 00:12:54.972
Come on. This crap ain't real. Ain't
nobody can track a demon like this.

00:12:59.035 --> 00:13:00.243
Our dad could.

00:13:03.258 --> 00:13:05.742
These are nonparametric
statistical overviews,

00:13:05.746 --> 00:13:08.782
Cross-Spectrum correlations. I mean...

00:13:09.495 --> 00:13:10.592
Damn!

00:13:12.026 --> 00:13:13.623
They're signs,

00:13:14.145 --> 00:13:17.690
Omens. If you can track them,
you can track this demon.

00:13:17.697 --> 00:13:21.631
You know, like crop
failures, electrical storms.

00:13:21.637 --> 00:13:25.562
You ever been struck by
lightning? It ain't fun.

00:13:25.565 --> 00:13:29.512
Can you track it or not?
Yeah, with this, I think so.

00:13:29.527 --> 00:13:32.600
But it's gonna take time. Give me...

00:13:34.435 --> 00:13:36.573
51 hours.

00:13:42.527 --> 00:13:43.870
Hey, man! Yeah?

00:13:43.885 --> 00:13:46.332
By the way, I dig the haircut.

00:13:47.525 --> 00:13:49.600
All business up front,

00:13:49.736 --> 00:13:51.401
Party in the back.

00:14:04.398 --> 00:14:05.850
Hey, Ellen, what is that?

00:14:06.975 --> 00:14:08.441
It's a police scanner.

00:14:08.447 --> 00:14:13.093
We keep tabs on things. No,
no, no, no. The... folder.

00:14:20.897 --> 00:14:23.400
I was gonna give this
to a friend of mine, but

00:14:24.305 --> 00:14:25.052
Take a look

00:14:25.058 --> 00:14:25.962
If you want.

00:14:27.756 --> 00:14:28.470
Thanks.

00:14:29.878 --> 00:14:31.843
How did your mom get
into this stuff, anyway?

00:14:31.848 --> 00:14:32.840
My dad.

00:14:33.077 --> 00:14:34.153
He was a hunter.

00:14:35.567 --> 00:14:36.802
He passed away.

00:14:38.555 --> 00:14:39.550
I'm sorry.

00:14:40.008 --> 00:14:41.203
It was a long time ago.

00:14:41.698 --> 00:14:42.861
I was just a kid.

00:14:44.878 --> 00:14:46.252
Sorry to hear about yo dad.

00:14:48.278 --> 00:14:49.120
Yeah.

00:14:52.145 --> 00:14:52.881
So,

00:14:54.025 --> 00:14:56.432
I guess I got 51 hours to waste.

00:14:56.728 --> 00:14:58.411
Maybe tonight we should...

00:15:04.917 --> 00:15:06.503
Oh, you know what? Never mind.

00:15:07.206 --> 00:15:09.603
What? Nothing, just...

00:15:11.028 --> 00:15:12.353
Wrong place, wrong time.

00:15:12.356 --> 00:15:14.823
I thought you were gonna toss
me some cheap pickup line.

00:15:14.828 --> 00:15:18.273
Most hunters come through that door,
think they can get in my pants with some

00:15:18.787 --> 00:15:21.891
Pizza, a six-Pack and
side one of "Zeppelin 4".

00:15:23.218 --> 00:15:25.012
What a bunch of scumbags.

00:15:26.525 --> 00:15:27.783
Not you.

00:15:29.026 --> 00:15:30.301
I guess not.

00:15:32.288 --> 00:15:33.833
Dean, come here. Check this out.

00:15:35.458 --> 00:15:36.440
Yeah.

00:15:37.508 --> 00:15:41.303
A few murders not far from
here that Ellen caught wind of.

00:15:41.305 --> 00:15:43.193
Looks to me like there might be a hunt.

00:15:43.196 --> 00:15:45.523
Yeah, so? So,

00:15:45.527 --> 00:15:47.030
I told her we'd check it out.

00:15:48.307 --> 00:15:50.650
You got to be kidding me. Killer clown?

00:15:50.655 --> 00:15:53.900
Yeah, he left the daughter
unharmed and killed the parents.

00:15:53.905 --> 00:15:55.370
Ripped them to pieces, actually.

00:15:55.376 --> 00:15:57.410
And this family was at
some carnival that night?

00:15:57.418 --> 00:16:00.042
Right, the Cooper carnival.

00:16:00.045 --> 00:16:02.840
How do you know we're not dealing
with some psycho carny in a clown suit?

00:16:02.845 --> 00:16:07.241
The cops have no leads, and all the
employees were tearing down shop...

00:16:07.247 --> 00:16:11.250
Alibis all around. Plus the girl said
she saw a clown vanish into thin air.

00:16:11.256 --> 00:16:14.692
Cops are saying trauma, of course.
I know what you're thinking, Sam.

00:16:14.698 --> 00:16:16.810
"Why did it have to be clowns?"

00:16:17.286 --> 00:16:18.663
Oh, give me a break.

00:16:18.666 --> 00:16:20.360
You didn't think I remembered, did you?

00:16:21.217 --> 00:16:25.082
Come on, you still bust out crying whenever
you see Ronald Mcdonald on the television.

00:16:25.095 --> 00:16:26.430
At least I'm not afraid of flying.

00:16:26.436 --> 00:16:28.920
Planes crash! And
apparently clowns kill.

00:16:32.737 --> 00:16:34.853
So, these types of murders,
they ever happen before?

00:16:35.407 --> 00:16:38.590
Uh, according to the file, 1981, the

00:16:38.596 --> 00:16:41.171
Bunker Brothers Circus.

00:16:41.176 --> 00:16:45.140
Same m.O. It happened three different
times, three different locales.

00:16:45.146 --> 00:16:49.593
It's weird though. If it is a spirit, it's usually
bound to a specific locale. A house or a town.

00:16:49.595 --> 00:16:52.260
How's this one moving from city
to city? Carnival to carnival?

00:16:52.265 --> 00:16:53.543
Cursed object, maybe.

00:16:53.825 --> 00:16:56.281
Spirit attaches itself
to something, and the

00:16:56.287 --> 00:17:00.381
Carnival carries it around.
Great. Paranormal scavenger hunt.

00:17:01.158 --> 00:17:03.173
This case was your idea.

00:17:03.178 --> 00:17:06.722
By the way, why is that? You were
awfully quick to jump on this job.

00:17:07.755 --> 00:17:10.040
So? So this is not like you, that's all.

00:17:10.567 --> 00:17:13.510
I thought you were hell-Bent
for leather on the demon hunt.

00:17:14.628 --> 00:17:15.942
I don't know. I just think

00:17:15.956 --> 00:17:18.823
Taking this job, it's what
dad would have wanted us to do.

00:17:19.265 --> 00:17:21.623
What dad would have wanted? Yeah.

00:17:22.948 --> 00:17:23.950
So?

00:17:28.006 --> 00:17:28.943
Nothing.

00:17:36.466 --> 00:17:37.680
Check it out.

00:17:41.028 --> 00:17:42.091
Evan, look.

00:17:43.226 --> 00:17:46.611
Scary! Yeah, dad, scary.

00:17:46.618 --> 00:17:47.613
What's over here?

00:17:54.017 --> 00:17:57.020
You know, when I was your age, this
would have scared the pants off me.

00:18:20.355 --> 00:18:21.343
Evan.

00:18:21.656 --> 00:18:22.472
Hey.

00:18:24.118 --> 00:18:25.032
What is it?

00:18:26.766 --> 00:18:28.001
I...

00:18:28.377 --> 00:18:29.762
I saw a clown.

00:18:32.118 --> 00:18:33.620
Don't be afraid of clowns.

00:18:33.937 --> 00:18:36.273
They're nice. They're your friends.

00:18:36.286 --> 00:18:38.472
Okay? Come on.

00:18:51.657 --> 00:18:52.681
Dad.

00:18:54.567 --> 00:18:55.552
Dad!

00:18:57.497 --> 00:18:58.343
Evan.

00:18:58.666 --> 00:18:59.713
What is it?

00:19:00.198 --> 00:19:01.922
You were right.

00:19:02.385 --> 00:19:03.913
He is my friend.

00:19:30.266 --> 00:19:31.281
Check it out.

00:19:31.288 --> 00:19:32.270
Five-O.

00:19:56.848 --> 00:19:57.771
Did you get her number?

00:20:02.315 --> 00:20:04.670
More murders? Two more last night.

00:20:04.676 --> 00:20:06.203
Apparently, they were ripped to shreds,

00:20:06.206 --> 00:20:08.000
And they had a little boy with them.

00:20:08.016 --> 00:20:09.730
Who fingered a clown.

00:20:13.756 --> 00:20:14.581
W hat?

00:20:15.228 --> 00:20:17.812
Yes, a clown, who apparently
vanished into thin air.

00:20:18.268 --> 00:20:20.820
Dean, you know, looking for
a cursed object, it's like

00:20:21.345 --> 00:20:24.360
Trying to find a needle in a stack
of needles. It could be anything.

00:20:25.225 --> 00:20:28.493
Well, it's bound to give off emf. So
we'll just have to scan everything.

00:20:28.495 --> 00:20:32.880
Oh, good. That's nice and inconspicuous.

00:20:33.128 --> 00:20:35.161
I guess we'll just have to blend in.

00:20:47.006 --> 00:20:48.033
Excuse me.

00:20:48.377 --> 00:20:50.471
We're looking for a Mr. Cooper.
Have you seen him around?

00:20:50.926 --> 00:20:52.670
What is that? Some kind of joke?

00:20:56.555 --> 00:20:58.820
Oh, god, I'm sorry. You think
I wouldn't give my eyeteeth

00:20:58.826 --> 00:21:03.440
To see Mr. Cooper or a
sunset or anything at all?

00:21:03.447 --> 00:21:04.711
Want to give me a little help here?

00:21:04.718 --> 00:21:05.670
Not really.

00:21:05.676 --> 00:21:07.680
Hey, Barry, is there a problem?

00:21:08.966 --> 00:21:12.620
Yeah, this guy hates
blind people. No, I don't.

00:21:12.625 --> 00:21:15.742
Hey, buddy, what's your problem? Nothing.
It's just a little misunderstanding.

00:21:15.748 --> 00:21:16.753
Little?

00:21:16.766 --> 00:21:18.711
You son of a bitch. No, no, no!

00:21:18.725 --> 00:21:21.083
Could somebody tell
me where Mr. Cooper is?

00:21:21.636 --> 00:21:22.831
Please?

00:21:22.837 --> 00:21:25.000
You boys picked a hell
of a time to join up.

00:21:25.195 --> 00:21:26.511
Take a seat.

00:21:27.068 --> 00:21:29.632
We got all kinds of local trouble.

00:21:31.406 --> 00:21:32.680
What do you mean?

00:21:32.778 --> 00:21:36.923
A couple of folks got themselves murdered.
Cops always seem to start here first.

00:21:36.928 --> 00:21:39.582
So, you two ever work
the circuit before?

00:21:39.585 --> 00:21:42.881
Uh, yes, sir. Last year
through Texas and Arkansas.

00:21:42.885 --> 00:21:44.520
Doing what?

00:21:45.227 --> 00:21:46.353
Ride jockeys?

00:21:46.768 --> 00:21:47.783
Pull shoot?

00:21:48.637 --> 00:21:50.672
A-And-S men?
Yeah, it's a...

00:21:50.925 --> 00:21:52.480
Little bit of everything, I guess.

00:21:55.167 --> 00:21:58.380
You two have never worked a show
in your lives before, have you?

00:21:59.615 --> 00:22:00.493
Nope.

00:22:01.467 --> 00:22:02.741
But we really need the work.

00:22:04.717 --> 00:22:06.823
And Sam here's got a
thing for the bearded lady.

00:22:11.617 --> 00:22:12.651
You see that picture?

00:22:13.835 --> 00:22:14.850
That's my daddy.

00:22:15.365 --> 00:22:16.401
You look just like him.

00:22:16.577 --> 00:22:17.861
He was in the business.

00:22:18.648 --> 00:22:21.542
Ran a freak show 'til they
outlawed them most places.

00:22:21.767 --> 00:22:25.270
Apparently displaying the
deformed isn't dignified.

00:22:25.276 --> 00:22:28.712
So, most of the performers went
from honest work to rotting in

00:22:28.718 --> 00:22:30.662
Hospitals and asylums.

00:22:31.955 --> 00:22:33.181
That's progress,

00:22:33.735 --> 00:22:34.702
I guess.

00:22:37.215 --> 00:22:38.561
You see, this place

00:22:38.636 --> 00:22:40.492
Is a refuge for outcasts.

00:22:40.657 --> 00:22:41.922
Always has been.

00:22:42.208 --> 00:22:44.501
For folks that don't
fit in nowhere else.

00:22:46.398 --> 00:22:47.310
But you two...

00:22:49.468 --> 00:22:51.183
You should go to school,

00:22:51.835 --> 00:22:53.132
Find a couple of girls,

00:22:53.428 --> 00:22:55.401
Have 2.5 kids,

00:22:55.407 --> 00:22:56.953
Live regular.

00:23:01.548 --> 00:23:02.473
Sir...

00:23:04.817 --> 00:23:06.012
We don't want to go to school.

00:23:06.435 --> 00:23:08.110
And we don't want regular.

00:23:08.867 --> 00:23:10.253
We want this.

00:23:14.275 --> 00:23:15.343
What?

00:23:16.687 --> 00:23:19.551
That whole "I don't want
to go back to school" thing,

00:23:19.755 --> 00:23:20.561
You just...

00:23:21.298 --> 00:23:23.533
You were just saying that
to Cooper, or were you,

00:23:23.878 --> 00:23:24.790
You know,

00:23:24.795 --> 00:23:25.712
Saying it?

00:23:27.708 --> 00:23:29.472
I don't know. You don't know?

00:23:30.486 --> 00:23:32.623
I thought that once the demon was dead

00:23:32.628 --> 00:23:35.820
And the fat lady sings that you were
gonna take off, head back to wussy state.

00:23:36.275 --> 00:23:37.602
I'm having second thoughts.

00:23:38.235 --> 00:23:40.010
Really? Yeah, I think...

00:23:41.838 --> 00:23:43.451
Dad would have wanted
me to stick to the job.

00:23:43.458 --> 00:23:45.280
Since when do you give
a damn what dad wanted?

00:23:45.708 --> 00:23:47.900
You spent half your life doing
exactly what he didn't want.

00:23:47.917 --> 00:23:49.662
Since he died, okay?

00:23:51.548 --> 00:23:53.023
You have a problem with that?

00:23:56.407 --> 00:23:57.802
No, I don't have a problem at all.

00:25:00.896 --> 00:25:01.992
Who is this?

00:25:39.766 --> 00:25:41.241
Hello? Hey, man.

00:25:42.035 --> 00:25:43.941
What's the matter? You sound
like you just saw a clown.

00:25:44.646 --> 00:25:45.612
Very funny.

00:25:47.695 --> 00:25:49.030
Skeleton, actually.

00:25:50.177 --> 00:25:52.571
Like a real human
skeleton? In the fun house.

00:25:52.577 --> 00:25:54.081
Listen, I was thinking. What if

00:25:54.087 --> 00:25:57.211
The spirit isn't attached to a cursed object.
What if it's attached to its own remains.

00:25:57.216 --> 00:25:59.570
Did the bones give off
emf? Well, no, but...

00:25:59.577 --> 00:26:01.613
We should check it out
anyway. I'm heading to you.

00:26:04.058 --> 00:26:06.341
What are you doing here, kid?

00:26:07.617 --> 00:26:09.943
Just sweeping. Bull.

00:26:09.945 --> 00:26:12.721
And what were you
talking about? Skeletons?

00:26:12.727 --> 00:26:14.373
What's emf?

00:26:15.466 --> 00:26:17.751
Dude, your blind-Man
hearing is out of control.

00:26:17.757 --> 00:26:19.931
We're a tight-Knit group.
We don't like outsiders.

00:26:19.936 --> 00:26:22.390
We take care of our own problems.

00:26:23.315 --> 00:26:25.511
We got a problem? You
tell me. You're the one

00:26:25.517 --> 00:26:27.892
Talking about human bones.

00:26:30.866 --> 00:26:32.173
Do you believe in ghosts?

00:26:32.766 --> 00:26:33.542
What?

00:26:33.716 --> 00:26:34.821
My brother and me...

00:26:36.867 --> 00:26:38.180
We're writing a book about them.

00:26:41.238 --> 00:26:42.990
What took you so long? Long story.

00:26:42.996 --> 00:26:44.972
Mommy, look at the clown.

00:26:47.467 --> 00:26:48.603
What clown?

00:26:53.125 --> 00:26:54.861
Come on, sweetie. Come on.

00:27:09.025 --> 00:27:10.503
Dean, I cannot believe

00:27:10.507 --> 00:27:12.833
You told Papasian about
the homicidal phantom clown.

00:27:12.836 --> 00:27:15.740
I told him an urban legend
about a homicidal phantom clown.

00:27:15.745 --> 00:27:17.153
I never said it was real. Keep it down.

00:27:19.358 --> 00:27:20.530
Oh, and get this.

00:27:20.538 --> 00:27:22.700
I mentioned the Bunker
Brothers Circus in '81

00:27:22.786 --> 00:27:25.680
And their evil-Clown
apocalypse. Guess what.

00:27:25.685 --> 00:27:26.473
What?

00:27:27.095 --> 00:27:29.111
Before Mr. Cooper owned Cooper carnival,

00:27:29.567 --> 00:27:30.952
He worked for the Bunker Brothers.

00:27:30.957 --> 00:27:32.151
He was their lot manager.

00:27:32.158 --> 00:27:34.070
So you think whatever's
the spirit attached to

00:27:34.088 --> 00:27:36.562
Cooper just brought it with
him? Something like that.

00:27:39.277 --> 00:27:41.370
I can't believe we keep
talking about clowns.

00:28:09.435 --> 00:28:11.391
Want to come in and play?

00:28:26.006 --> 00:28:29.391
Want to see mommy and
daddy? They're upstairs.

00:28:31.336 --> 00:28:32.433
Hey!

00:28:42.088 --> 00:28:43.792
Sam, watch out!

00:28:48.215 --> 00:28:49.833
What's going on in here?

00:28:49.838 --> 00:28:52.091
Oh, my god! What do you do to my
daughter! Get away from my kid!

00:28:52.095 --> 00:28:55.062
Mommy, daddy, they shot my clown.

00:29:05.576 --> 00:29:07.122
You really think they saw our plates?

00:29:08.916 --> 00:29:10.422
I don't want to take the chance.

00:29:10.598 --> 00:29:12.622
Besides, I hate this
freaking thing anyway.

00:29:14.775 --> 00:29:16.433
Well, one thing's for sure.

00:29:16.435 --> 00:29:17.421
What's that?

00:29:18.196 --> 00:29:19.621
We're not dealing with a spirit.

00:29:19.946 --> 00:29:21.720
That rock salt hit something solid.

00:29:21.918 --> 00:29:25.530
Yeah, a person, or maybe a creature
that can make itself invisible?

00:29:25.545 --> 00:29:27.550
Yeah, and dresses up
like a clown for kicks?

00:29:27.555 --> 00:29:28.990
Did it say anything in dad's journal?

00:29:29.007 --> 00:29:29.701
Nope.

00:29:33.288 --> 00:29:34.060
Who you calling?

00:29:34.485 --> 00:29:37.022
Maybe Ellen or that guy
Ash will know something.

00:29:37.785 --> 00:29:39.461
Hey, you think, uh...

00:29:40.058 --> 00:29:42.023
You think dad and
Ellen ever had a thing?

00:29:42.328 --> 00:29:43.253
No way.

00:29:43.545 --> 00:29:45.321
Then why didn't he tell us about her?

00:29:45.706 --> 00:29:47.780
I don't know. Maybe they
had some sort of falling-Out.

00:29:48.708 --> 00:29:49.570
Yeah.

00:29:51.918 --> 00:29:54.551
You ever notice dad had a
falling-Out with just about everybody?

00:29:59.288 --> 00:30:00.912
Don't get all maudlin on me, man.

00:30:00.915 --> 00:30:01.743
What do you mean?

00:30:02.347 --> 00:30:06.160
I mean this strong, silent thing
of yours. It's crap. I'm over it.

00:30:06.165 --> 00:30:08.443
This isn't just anyone we're
talking about. This is dad.

00:30:08.446 --> 00:30:10.163
I know how you felt about the man.

00:30:10.165 --> 00:30:13.351
Back off, all right? Just because I'm
not caring and sharing like you want...

00:30:13.355 --> 00:30:16.293
No, no, no. That's not what this is about,
Dean. I don't care how you deal with this,

00:30:16.295 --> 00:30:18.080
But you have to deal with it, man.

00:30:19.586 --> 00:30:21.890
Listen, I'm your brother, all right?
I just want to make sure you're okay.

00:30:21.898 --> 00:30:23.782
Dude, I'm okay! I'm okay!

00:30:23.787 --> 00:30:25.892
I swear, the next person
who asks me if I'm okay,

00:30:25.896 --> 00:30:27.400
I'm gonna start throwing punches.

00:30:27.595 --> 00:30:29.913
These are your issues.
Quit dumping them on me.

00:30:29.915 --> 00:30:30.860
What are you talking about?

00:30:30.875 --> 00:30:33.702
I just think it's really interesting
this sudden obedience you have to dad.

00:30:33.706 --> 00:30:35.563
It's like, "oh, what
would dad want me to do?"

00:30:35.945 --> 00:30:38.371
You spent your entire life
slugging it out with that man.

00:30:38.377 --> 00:30:41.000
I mean, hell, you picked a fight with
him the last time you ever saw him,

00:30:41.006 --> 00:30:43.041
And now that he's dead,
now you wanna make it right?

00:30:43.045 --> 00:30:45.602
Well, I'm sorry, Sam, but you
can't. It's too little too late.

00:30:45.606 --> 00:30:46.753
Why are you saying this to me?

00:30:46.757 --> 00:30:50.511
I want you to be honest with yourself
about this! I'm dealing with dad's death.

00:30:50.985 --> 00:30:51.882
Are you?

00:30:57.748 --> 00:30:58.811
I'm gonna call Ellen.

00:31:10.587 --> 00:31:11.682
Thanks a lot.

00:31:13.866 --> 00:31:15.151
Rakshasa.

00:31:15.757 --> 00:31:18.102
What's that? Ellen's best guess.

00:31:18.447 --> 00:31:22.121
It's a race of ancient hindu
creatures. They appear in human form,

00:31:22.128 --> 00:31:24.083
They feed on human flesh,

00:31:24.397 --> 00:31:26.092
They can make themselves invisible,

00:31:26.096 --> 00:31:28.871
And they cannot enter a home
without first being invited to.

00:31:28.876 --> 00:31:31.421
They dress up like clowns,
and children invite them in.

00:31:31.426 --> 00:31:33.683
Why don't they just munch
on the kids? No idea.

00:31:33.868 --> 00:31:35.332
Not enough meat on the bones, maybe?

00:31:35.336 --> 00:31:38.673
What else you find out? Apparently,
rakshasas live in squalor.

00:31:39.045 --> 00:31:41.741
They sleep on a bed of dead insects.

00:31:42.638 --> 00:31:45.433
And they have to feed a few
times. Every 20 to 30 years.

00:31:45.437 --> 00:31:47.850
Slow metabolism, I
guess. That makes sense.

00:31:47.856 --> 00:31:50.850
The carnival today, the
Bunker Brothers in '81.

00:31:50.858 --> 00:31:53.111
Probably more before that.

00:31:53.315 --> 00:31:55.450
Sam, who do we know
that worked both shows?

00:31:55.455 --> 00:31:57.121
Cooper? Cooper.

00:31:58.458 --> 00:32:00.320
You know, that picture of his father,

00:32:00.588 --> 00:32:01.810
That looked just like him.

00:32:02.748 --> 00:32:04.082
You think maybe it was him?

00:32:04.967 --> 00:32:06.723
Well, who knows how old he is?

00:32:06.727 --> 00:32:08.041
Ellen say how to kill him?

00:32:08.525 --> 00:32:11.540
Legend goes a dagger made of pure brass.

00:32:13.587 --> 00:32:15.493
I think I know where
to get one of those.

00:32:15.497 --> 00:32:18.701
Well, before we go stabbing things into Cooper,
we're gonna want to make damn sure it's him.

00:32:18.707 --> 00:32:21.383
Oh, you're such a stickler
for details, Sammy.

00:32:22.076 --> 00:32:23.872
All right, I'll round up the blade.

00:32:24.118 --> 00:32:26.250
You go check if Cooper's got bedbugs.

00:32:47.827 --> 00:32:50.372
Well, I got all kinds of knives.

00:32:50.665 --> 00:32:53.210
I don't know if I got
a brass one, though.

00:33:01.886 --> 00:33:03.000
What do you think you're doing?

00:33:05.318 --> 00:33:06.601
Check the trunk.

00:33:23.486 --> 00:33:24.353
You?

00:33:28.606 --> 00:33:29.711
Me.

00:33:43.265 --> 00:33:44.371
All right!

00:33:45.655 --> 00:33:46.860
Jeez.

00:33:49.077 --> 00:33:50.080
Hey!

00:33:50.756 --> 00:33:51.541
Hey!

00:33:52.426 --> 00:33:55.112
So, Cooper thinks I'm a
peeping tom, but it's not him.

00:33:55.116 --> 00:33:56.361
Yeah, so I gathered.

00:33:56.378 --> 00:33:58.102
It's the blind guy. He's here somewhere.

00:33:58.106 --> 00:34:00.282
Well, did you get...
The brass blades? No.

00:34:00.288 --> 00:34:01.840
It's just been one of those days.

00:34:03.106 --> 00:34:04.761
I got an idea. Come on.

00:34:16.378 --> 00:34:18.143
Dean, find the maze, okay?

00:34:58.055 --> 00:34:58.990
Where is it? I don't know.

00:34:58.996 --> 00:35:00.731
Shouldn't we see his
clothes walking around?

00:35:15.607 --> 00:35:17.603
Dean, where is it? I don't know!

00:35:31.907 --> 00:35:34.170
Sam, behind you!

00:36:01.127 --> 00:36:02.731
I hate fun houses.

00:36:18.068 --> 00:36:19.533
You boys did a hell of a job.

00:36:19.698 --> 00:36:21.560
Your dad would be proud. Thanks.

00:36:30.338 --> 00:36:32.512
Oh, yeah, I've got to, uh...

00:36:34.308 --> 00:36:35.601
I've got to go...

00:36:36.037 --> 00:36:37.273
Over there...

00:36:37.555 --> 00:36:38.811
Right now.

00:36:43.706 --> 00:36:45.550
So. So.

00:36:47.155 --> 00:36:48.431
Am I gonna see you again?

00:36:51.325 --> 00:36:52.443
Do you want to?

00:36:54.495 --> 00:36:55.750
I wouldn't hate it.

00:36:56.556 --> 00:36:57.792
Can I be honest with you?

00:36:58.087 --> 00:36:59.202
See, normally,

00:36:59.206 --> 00:37:01.733
I'd be hitting on you so
fast it'd make your head spin.

00:37:02.098 --> 00:37:03.123
But

00:37:04.585 --> 00:37:05.781
These days...

00:37:06.946 --> 00:37:07.773
I don't know.

00:37:08.338 --> 00:37:09.413
Wrong place,

00:37:10.145 --> 00:37:11.500
Wrong time?

00:37:13.087 --> 00:37:14.360
It's okay. I get it.

00:37:17.698 --> 00:37:19.691
Where you guys been?

00:37:19.837 --> 00:37:22.800
I've been waiting for you.
We were working a job, Ash.

00:37:24.118 --> 00:37:26.402
Clowns? Clowns? What the...

00:37:26.408 --> 00:37:27.592
You got something for us, Ash?

00:37:28.507 --> 00:37:29.911
Did you find the demon?

00:37:30.125 --> 00:37:31.321
It's nowhere around,

00:37:31.525 --> 00:37:33.240
At least nowhere I can find.

00:37:33.256 --> 00:37:36.010
But if this fugly
bastard raises its head,

00:37:36.508 --> 00:37:40.273
I'll know. I mean, I'm on
it like divine on dog dookie.

00:37:40.275 --> 00:37:41.212
What do you mean?

00:37:41.998 --> 00:37:43.241
I mean

00:37:43.968 --> 00:37:47.121
Any of those signs or omens
appear anywhere in the world,

00:37:47.125 --> 00:37:49.982
My rig will go off like a fire alarm.

00:37:50.855 --> 00:37:51.962
You mind?

00:37:56.395 --> 00:37:57.422
What's up, man?

00:37:59.388 --> 00:38:01.251
Ash, where did you learn to do all this?

00:38:01.258 --> 00:38:05.382
M.I.T., before I got
bounced for fighting.

00:38:07.646 --> 00:38:08.623
M.I.T.?

00:38:08.895 --> 00:38:10.270
It's a school in Boston.

00:38:11.176 --> 00:38:11.981
Okay.

00:38:12.585 --> 00:38:14.133
Give us a call as soon
as you know something?

00:38:14.715 --> 00:38:16.403
S, s, compadre.

00:38:27.556 --> 00:38:28.911
Hey, listen.

00:38:29.746 --> 00:38:32.700
If you boys need a place to stay,
I got a couple beds out back.

00:38:34.217 --> 00:38:35.340
Thanks, but no.

00:38:36.547 --> 00:38:38.151
There's something I got to finish.

00:38:38.158 --> 00:38:38.983
Okay.

00:38:54.297 --> 00:38:55.172
You were right.

00:38:56.708 --> 00:38:57.592
About what?

00:39:02.256 --> 00:39:03.311
About me and dad.

00:39:04.297 --> 00:39:07.203
I'm sorry that the last time I was
with him, I tried to pick a fight.

00:39:07.637 --> 00:39:10.010
I'm sorry that I spent most
of my life angry at him.

00:39:10.157 --> 00:39:11.862
I mean, for all I know, he died

00:39:11.988 --> 00:39:13.320
Thinking that I hate him.

00:39:15.516 --> 00:39:16.672
So, you're right.

00:39:18.818 --> 00:39:21.013
What I'm doing right
now... It is too little.

00:39:23.216 --> 00:39:24.213
It's too late.

00:39:29.658 --> 00:39:31.061
I miss him, man.

00:39:34.026 --> 00:39:35.631
And I feel guilty as hell.

00:39:39.515 --> 00:39:40.892
And I'm not all right...

00:39:42.956 --> 00:39:44.011
Not at all...

00:39:52.745 --> 00:39:53.940
But neither are you.

00:39:55.726 --> 00:39:56.793
That much I know.

00:40:01.135 --> 00:40:02.613
I'll let you get back to work.



00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
